[
  {
    "name": "azul_widgets_touch_tabs_pictures_a_strip_in_the_status_bar_around_the_camera",
    "description": "The pictures of the tab strip in the status bar's band (QA's contact sheet: tabs/): the window is a Pixel 8 (411 x 914 dp) with the camera in the middle, light and dark, flat and flora, a pill far along the row selected (the row scrolls to put it whole in a lane), the phone on its side, an iPhone with the Dynamic Island, a ribbon's tabs as the strip (AzWriter), and the same page with no phone (three tabs and twelve, the flip panel). Every picture is a CPU render of the window at rest, taken in this order: 1 Pixel 8 portrait light flat, 2 Design selected, 3 Account selected (the end of the row), 4 dark, 5 flora light, 6 flora dark, 7 iPhone island portrait, 8 iPhone island landscape, 9 Pixel 8 landscape, 10 ribbon in the band, 11 ribbon, Review selected, 12 ribbon dark, 13 no phone: three tabs, 14 no phone: twelve tabs and the flip panel. The assertions are the page's own: they keep the scenario honest on every platform.",
